## Story Description
Three additive changes so unit_price flows from ingestion through to the rules engine. (1) Add unit_price: Optional[float] = None and unit_of_measure: Optional[str] = None to CanonicalTransaction in src/models/schema.py after the abc_segment field. (2) Add Column('unit_price', Float, nullable=True) and Column('unit_of_measure', Text, nullable=True) to transactions_table in src/models/database.py after the existing source_raw_id column. (3) Add 'unit_price' and 'unit_of_measure' to the _DB_COLUMNS set in src/ingestion/ingest.py so these columns pass through the _df_to_records filter.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: src/models/schema.py — in CanonicalTransaction class, after the line 'abc_segment: Optional[str] = None', add two new lines: 'unit_price: Optional[float] = None' and 'unit_of_measure: Optional[str] = None'
- Edit file: src/models/database.py — in transactions_table Table definition, after the line "Column('source_raw_id', Text, nullable=True),", add: "Column('unit_price', Float, nullable=True)," and "Column('unit_of_measure', Text, nullable=True),"
- Edit file: src/ingestion/ingest.py — in the _DB_COLUMNS set definition (lines starting with the set literal), add 'unit_price' and 'unit_of_measure' to the set
- Run: python -c "from src.models.schema import CanonicalTransaction; t = CanonicalTransaction(source_system='T', source_row_number=1, invoice_number='I', original_amount=1, original_currency='AUD', base_amount=1, base_currency='AUD', raw_data={}); print(t.unit_price, t.unit_of_measure)" — should print None None without error
- Run: python -c "from src.models.database import transactions_table; cols = [c.name for c in transactions_table.columns]; assert 'unit_price' in cols and 'unit_of_measure' in cols; print('OK')" — should print OK

